  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "We can combine transformations by applying them in turn.\n\nFor example, suppose that the segment $\\overline{AB}$ below is dilated with center $O$ and a scale factor $2,$ and then shifted $3$ units down. What is the resulting segment? \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/bc65e4edde561add5403cf57abc2cba50eabc4a9f7b8ba7592a0ea1f4f95c576.png)\n\nLet's apply the transformations in turn.\n\n- Dilating with center $O$ and scale factor $2$ gives the segment $\\overline{A'B'},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/c526ed621e357ce098c420d3ef5912f347c13bd5c898ca5a2a165570607ea1fd.png)\n\n- Next, we take $\\overline{A'B'}$ and shift it by $3$ units down. This gives the segment $\\overline{A''B''}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223522/assets/a78807d3f1fb43f3773671f7c4f5696dd3779ae9ce1d8da797377c3574170a92.png)",
